    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39646" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">purpŭrātus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		purpura, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>clad in purple</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulier,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most. 1, 3, 131</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> As
				<i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">purpŭrātus</span></b> , i,
				m., <i>a high officer at a king's
			court</i> (so called because clothed in purple), <i><span class="en">Cic.
				Tusc. 1, 43, 102</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 30,
			42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">37, 23</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Flor.
				1, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Curt. 3, 2, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 6,
			4</span></i>.—Hence, sarcastically of Gabinius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Cat.
				4, 6, 12</span></i>.</div>
